  "source_path": "/scratch/ziv_baretto/Thesis_Ziv/Capstone-Thesis-/DATA_SET_BUILDER_AND_EXPLORER/Timeline_Maker/output_merged_v3/food_safety/Pandian ... Revision vs State Represented By on 30 January, 2019.json",
  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Pandian ...",
    "facts": "He has filed this Criminal Revision Case to [LEAKAGE_MASK] the conviction dated 09.11.2009 in Crl.A.No.72 of 2009 passed by the learned Additional Sessions Judge, Fast Track Court No.II, Thoothukudi, confirming the conviction and the sentence Pandian ... respondent police has filed charge sheet against the revision petitioner herein for the offences punishable under Sections 7(i) and 16(i)(a)(i) and (ii) r/w 2 (ia) (a) and (m) of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954 before the learned Judicial Magistrate, Sathankulam. Aggrieved against the same, the petitioner / accused has approached this Court by way of filing this Criminal Revision Case.",
    "arguments": "6.The learned counsel appearing for the revision petitioner would submit that both the Courts below have miserably failed to see that there is a considerable delay in lodging the prosecution for the alleged adulteration of Maida, which said to have been contained 0.33% Alcoholic Acidity as against permitted limitation of 0.12% as per Ex.P.13, report of the Lab, which is said to have been received on 19.04.2004 in Form 13. However, the complaint for prosecution has been lodged before the competent Jurisdictional Court on 10.07.2006 with delay of almost two years and copy of Ex.P.13, lab test has been served upon the accused on 12.08.2006, which according to the revision petitioner is violation of the mandatory statutory period, http://www.judis.nic.in namely, beyond period of 10 days as prescribed in Rule 9(B) of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954. 7.He also relied upon the following decisions in the case of:- (i) State by Food Inspector, Cumbam... Vs. Jafar Ali on 06.02.2004. (ii) State by Food Inspector, Trichy Vs. Paulraj, on 11.02.2004. 9.Heard the learned counsel appearing for the petitioner, the learned Government Advocate (Crl.Side) appearing for the respondent and perused the materials available on record carefully. 10.Point for consideration in this Criminal Revision Case is that whether the right of the accused in sending the sample taken by the prosecution to Central Food Laboratory at the instance of the accused has been vitiated or withheld due to deliberate delay in lodging the prosecution or not?.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "6.The learned counsel appearing for the revision petitioner would submit that both the Courts below have miserably failed to see that there is a considerable delay in lodging the prosecution for the alleged adulteration of Maida, which said to have been contained 0.33% Alcoholic Acidity as against permitted limitation of 0.12% as per Ex.P.13, report of the Lab, which is said to have been received on 19.04.2004 in Form 13. However, the complaint for prosecution has been lodged before the competent Jurisdictional Court on 10.07.2006 with delay of almost two years and copy of Ex.P.13, lab test has been served upon the accused on 12.08.2006, which according to the revision petitioner is violation of the mandatory statutory period, http://www.judis.nic.in namely, beyond period of 10 days as prescribed in Rule 9(B) of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954. 7.He also relied upon the following decisions in the case of:- (i) State by Food Inspector, Cumbam... Vs. Jafar Ali on 06.02.2004. (ii) State by Food Inspector, Trichy Vs. Paulraj, on 11.02.2004. 9.Heard the learned counsel appearing for the petitioner, the learned Government Advocate (Crl.Side) appearing for the respondent and perused the materials available on record carefully. 10.Point for consideration in this Criminal Revision Case is that whether the right of the accused in sending the sample taken by the prosecution to Central Food Laboratory at the instance of the accused has been vitiated or withheld due to deliberate delay in lodging the prosecution or not?.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
